// a self-recursive type made finite by an absent `@optional`
// XTypes 1.3 §7.3.1.2.1.3 (`@optional`) and Table 21 (`@external`).
// The cycle passes through no collection; what terminates it is the
// member being absent, the same way a sequence's length terminates one.
//
// The forward declaration is written even though IDL 4.2 §7.5 puts
// `Node` in scope from the start of its own declaration: four of the
// six implementations answered "`Node` was not defined previously" to
// the form without it, and this is the spelling that gives them the
// declaration they ask for.
module m {
  struct Node;

  @mutable struct Node {
    long value;
    @optional @external Node next;
  };
};
